<dc:title>&quot;I Have a Dream&quot; Inscription</dc:title>
<dc:description>Eighteen steps from the top landing of the &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/33&quot;&gt;Lincoln Memorial&lt;/a&gt;, an inscription marks the spot where &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/90&quot;&gt;Dr. Martin Luther King Jr&lt;/a&gt;. stood to give his &quot;I Have a Dream&quot; speech in 1963. The marker was placed in 2003 to mark the 40th anniversary of that speech. Coretta Scott King, Dr. King&#039;s widow, attended and spoke at the dedication.</dc:description>
<dc:source>Internal archive, National Park Service.</dc:source>
<dc:date>08/22/2003 (Dedicated)</dc:date>
